=== NON-BLOCKING FINDINGS (reported, not grounds for FAIL) ===
N1 (coverage gap, criterion 6 probe). BITE 3 (scratchpad/bite3, fresh copy):
   mutating the OTHER phase-dollar call site --
   spending-phases.html:78 {{formatDollars (mul $phase.Multiplier
   $.Settings.MonthlyLivingExpenses)}} -> ${{formatNumber (mul ...)}} --
   leaves the oracle GREEN (passed=8 failed=0, ORACLE PASS, exit 0) and the
   whole suite green (`go test ./internal/handlers/whatif/
   ./internal/templates/` -> ok). The oracle's TestOracleW2PhaseDollarLabels
   and the worker's tie test both render "whatif-quick-adjust-phases-content"
   only; nothing renders "whatif-spending-phases" and asserts its
   .phase-dollar-label. The shipped code is nonetheless CORRECT there --
   checker-planted zz_checker_sp_test.go renders "whatif-spending-phases"
   with 7386 x 1.25 and gets phase-dollar-label = "$9,233/mo" (canonical,
   not %.0f's $9,232). So the criterion "server uses formatDollars on
   phase-dollar labels in spending-phases.html" is met by direct
   observation; only its regression guard is missing. Criterion 6 as written
   ("revert one server call site ... must FAIL") is satisfied by bites 1
   and 2.
N2 (structural, no behavioral divergence). rate-assumptions.html:866 still
   formats a whole-dollar figure inline:
     <td ...>$${Math.round(spending).toLocaleString()}/mo</td>
   rather than calling formatWholeDollars. This is a second whole-dollar
   formatting expression, at odds with the spec's "used by all JS
   whole-dollar recomputations"; the oracle's check 03 is scoped to
   quick-adjust-scripts.html and cannot see it. It is however byte-identical
   to formatWholeDollars ('$' + Math.round(v).toLocaleString()):
   cmd: node -e '<compare both over 7386, 7386.5, 7386.55, 8124.6, 9232.5,
        0, 0.5, 1234567.5, 10000/7>'  -> divergences=0
   and harness3 proved the rendered row is the canonical "$7,386/mo" from
   the exact base. The brief's own enumeration for criterion (5)/(3)
   ("currency/phase-dollar/aria paths and portfolio-settings' inline code")
   does not list this path, so I do not fail on it. Exactly one
   `function formatWholeDollars` exists across web/templates (grep -rn).
   The three remaining bare .toLocaleString() calls in
   healthcare-person.html format healthcare premiums, not
   MonthlyLivingExpenses, and are outside W2's value scope.
N3 (harness limitation, disclosed). jsdom does not apply a range input's
   step sanitisation, so it reported primary.value === "7386.00" at load
   where a real browser would show 7400. Real-browser snapping was NOT
   directly observed by any command I ran; I compensated by forcing
   primary.value='7400' by hand (harness2 E0b) before exercising every JS
   read path. The server-side half of the snap trap is covered by the
   on-disk round-trip under criterion 4.
N4 (noise). Under jsdom an unrelated inline script threw
   "window.matchMedia is not a function" (dark-mode init). It is a jsdom
   API gap, not a page defect, and it did not prevent the quick-adjust /
   phase / preview scripts from running -- all 44 harness assertions across
   the three harnesses passed.
